IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part VIII.4 (Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit):
-- Employment Insurance Emergency Response Benefit (ss 153.7 to 153.11) and the Operating Account (s 153.111).
-- Written by piece ei6 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30; nothing here is
-- claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- Seat: a person who has lost work or cannot work and asks whether they qualify for the benefit, how much they get,
-- for how long, and what they must do or tell the Commission.
--
-- THE CLAIMANT is the person of s 153.5(2) (module ei6-part-8-4-claimant); here "claimant" is a BOOLEAN input.
-- Every rule has its own GIVEN, because the stable binary rejects a GIVEN on a section.
-- Part VIII.4 was added by Interim Orders and ceases to apply under s 153.14 on June 2, 2027 at the latest. Every date
-- a rule of this module allows is in 2020, so none of them takes the s 153.14 date (fork F-ei6-9 in NOTES.md).

§ `Section 153.7 - payment of the benefit`

-- src:2807 | 153.7 (1) An employment insurance emergency response benefit is payable to a claimant who makes a claim under section 153.8 and who is eligible for the benefit.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.7(1) (src:2807)
GIVEN `a claimant within the meaning of Part VIII.4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `makes a claim under section 153.8` IS A BOOLEAN
      `eligible for the benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.7(1) the emergency response benefit is payable to the claimant` IF
        `a claimant within the meaning of Part VIII.4`
    AND `makes a claim under section 153.8`
    AND `eligible for the benefit`

-- (1.1): a permission of the Commission, so a no-right of the claimant to be paid at the customary time only.
-- src:2809 | (1.1) The Commission may pay the employment insurance emergency response benefit in advance of the customary time for paying it.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.7(1.1) (src:2809)
GIVEN `the payment is of the employment insurance emergency response benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.7(1.1) the Commission may pay the benefit before the customary time for paying it` IF
    `the payment is of the employment insurance emergency response benefit`

-- (2) and (3): receiving the money or financial aid changes nothing about eligibility. The receipt is a parameter that
-- is deliberately not read: the answer is the eligibility the claimant had without it.
-- src:2811 | (2) A claimant who receives, under a provincial Act or any other provincial mechanism, a sum of money or financial aid of any type and in any form, for reasons related to COVID-19, remains eligible to receive the employment insurance emergency response benefit.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.7(2) (src:2811)
GIVEN `eligible apart from the provincial money or financial aid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `receives under a provincial Act or other provincial mechanism a sum of money or financial aid for reasons related to COVID-19` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.7(2) the claimant remains eligible despite provincial money or financial aid` IF
    `eligible apart from the provincial money or financial aid`

-- src:2813 | (3) A claimant who receives financial aid as a result of entering into an agreement referred to in section 63 remains eligible to receive the employment insurance emergency response benefit.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.7(3) (src:2813)
GIVEN `eligible apart from the financial aid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `receives financial aid as a result of entering into an agreement referred to in section 63` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.7(3) the claimant remains eligible despite financial aid under section 63` IF
    `eligible apart from the financial aid`

§ `Section 153.8 - the claim`

-- The days of s 153.8, carried as values (dates are data).
-- src:2815 | 153.8 (1) Any claimant may, in the form and manner established by the Minister, make a claim for the employment insurance emergency response benefit for any two-week period starting on a Sunday and falling within the period beginning on March 15, 2020 and ending on October 3, 2020.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.8(1) (src:2815)
GIVETH A `Period of days`
`s 153.8(1) the period within which the two-week period must fall` MEANS
    `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15), (YearMonthDay 2020 10 3)

-- src:2817 | (1.1) Despite subsection (1), an employment insurance emergency response benefit is not payable to a claimant for the week beginning September 27, 2020 unless an employment insurance emergency response benefit was paid or payable to the claimant for any week beginning before that date.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.8(1.1) (src:2817)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 153.8(1.1) the Sunday that begins the week of the exception` MEANS YearMonthDay 2020 9 27

-- src:2819 | (2) A claim must not be made after December 2, 2020.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.8(2) (src:2819)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 153.8(2) the last day on which a claim may be made` MEANS YearMonthDay 2020 12 2

-- (1): a claim for "any two-week period starting on a Sunday and falling within" March 15 to October 3, 2020.
-- A two-week period is 14 days: the first day plus 13. "Falling within" is read as: the whole period lies inside, so
-- the last two-week period that fits begins on Sunday September 20 (fork F-ei6-2 in NOTES.md).
-- src:2815 | 153.8 (1) Any claimant may, in the form and manner established by the Minister, make a claim for the employment insurance emergency response benefit for any two-week period starting on a Sunday and falling within the period beginning on March 15, 2020 and ending on October 3, 2020.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.8(1) (src:2815)
GIVEN `the first day of the two-week period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.8(1) the two-week period starts on a Sunday and falls within the period` IF
        `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` `the first day of the two-week period` EQUALS `the first day of the two-week period`
    AND `the day` `the first day of the two-week period` `falls within` `s 153.8(1) the period within which the two-week period must fall`
    AND `the day` (`the first day of the two-week period` PLUS 13) `falls within` `s 153.8(1) the period within which the two-week period must fall`

-- src:2815 | 153.8 (1) Any claimant may, in the form and manner established by the Minister, make a claim for the employment insurance emergency response benefit for any two-week period starting on a Sunday and falling within the period beginning on March 15, 2020 and ending on October 3, 2020.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.8(1) (src:2815)
GIVEN `a claimant within the meaning of Part VIII.4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is made in the form and manner established by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the two-week period starts on a Sunday and falls within the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.8(1) the claimant may make a claim for the two-week period` IF
        `a claimant within the meaning of Part VIII.4`
    AND `the claim is made in the form and manner established by the Minister`
    AND `the two-week period starts on a Sunday and falls within the period`

-- (1.1): the benefit is not payable for the week beginning September 27, 2020 unless it was paid or payable for a
-- week beginning before that date. For every other week this subsection bars nothing.
-- src:2817 | (1.1) Despite subsection (1), an employment insurance emergency response benefit is not payable to a claimant for the week beginning September 27, 2020 unless an employment insurance emergency response benefit was paid or payable to the claimant for any week beginning before that date.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.8(1.1) (src:2817)
GIVEN `the Sunday that begins the week` IS A DATE
      `the benefit was paid or payable for a week beginning before September 27, 2020` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.8(1.1) the benefit is not barred for the week` IF
        NOT (`the Sunday that begins the week` EQUALS `s 153.8(1.1) the Sunday that begins the week of the exception`)
     OR `the benefit was paid or payable for a week beginning before September 27, 2020`

-- src:2819 | (2) A claim must not be made after December 2, 2020.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.8(2) (src:2819)
GIVEN `the day on which the claim is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.8(2) the claim is made in time` IF
    `the day on which the claim is made` AT MOST `s 153.8(2) the last day on which a claim may be made`

-- (3) and (4): the claimant's duty and the employer's duty to give the Minister information the Minister requires; the
-- Minister's right to it. The consequence for a claimant who does not is s 50(1) as adapted (ei6-part-8-4-administration).
-- src:2821 | (3) A claimant must provide the Minister with any information that the Minister may require in respect of the claim.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.8(3) (src:2821)
GIVEN `the Minister requires information in respect of the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.8(3) the claimant must provide the Minister with the information` IF
    `the Minister requires information in respect of the claim`

-- src:2823 | (4) An employer must provide the Minister with any information that the Minister may require in respect of the claim.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.8(4) (src:2823)
GIVEN `the Minister requires information in respect of the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.8(4) the employer must provide the Minister with the information` IF
    `the Minister requires information in respect of the claim`

-- (5) and (6): no benefit period is to be established, with respect to a benefit referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a),
-- for a benefit period beginning in the two periods below. The day tested is the day the benefit period would begin
-- (assumed, not ruled: fork F-ei6-3 in NOTES.md).
-- src:2825 | (5) For the period beginning on March 15, 2020 and ending on September 26, 2020, no benefit period is to be established with respect to any of the benefits referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.8(5) (src:2825)
GIVETH A `Period of days`
`s 153.8(5) the period in which no benefit period is to be established` MEANS
    `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15), (YearMonthDay 2020 9 26)

-- src:2827 | (6) For the period beginning on September 27, 2020 and ending on October 3, 2020, no benefit period is to be established with respect to any of the benefits referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a) if
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.8(6) (src:2827)
GIVETH A `Period of days`
`s 153.8(6) the period in which no benefit period is to be established if the conditions are met` MEANS
    `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2020 9 27), (YearMonthDay 2020 10 3)

-- src:2825 | (5) For the period beginning on March 15, 2020 and ending on September 26, 2020, no benefit period is to be established with respect to any of the benefits referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a).
-- src:2826 | No benefit period — September 27 to October 3, 2020
-- src:2827 | (6) For the period beginning on September 27, 2020 and ending on October 3, 2020, no benefit period is to be established with respect to any of the benefits referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a) if
-- src:2828 | (a) an employment insurance emergency response benefit was paid or payable to the claimant for any week beginning before September 27, 2020; and
-- src:2829 | (b) the claimant has not claimed the employment insurance emergency response benefit for the maximum number of weeks referred to in section 153.11.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.8(5), (6) (src:2825-2829)
GIVEN `the first day of the benefit period that would be established` IS A DATE
      `the benefit is one referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefit was paid or payable for a week beginning before September 27, 2020` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of weeks for which the claimant has claimed the benefit` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum number of weeks referred to in section 153.11` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.8(5) and (6) no benefit period is to be established` IF
        `the benefit is one referred to in paragraph 153.5(3)(a)`
    AND (   `the day` `the first day of the benefit period that would be established` `falls within` `s 153.8(5) the period in which no benefit period is to be established`
         OR (    `the day` `the first day of the benefit period that would be established` `falls within` `s 153.8(6) the period in which no benefit period is to be established if the conditions are met`
             AND `the benefit was paid or payable for a week beginning before September 27, 2020`
             AND `the number of weeks for which the claimant has claimed the benefit` LESS THAN `the maximum number of weeks referred to in section 153.11`))

-- (7): on receiving a claim the Commission shall decide whether the claimant is eligible and whether the benefit is
-- payable for the two-week period, and notify the claimant. The claimant's claim is to a decision and a notice.
-- src:2831 | (7) On receiving a claim for the employment insurance emergency response benefit, the Commission shall decide whether the claimant is eligible for the benefit and whether the benefit is payable to the claimant for the two-week period in respect of which they claimed the benefit, and shall notify the claimant of its decisions in any manner that it considers adequate.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.8(7) (src:2831)
GIVEN `the Commission has received a claim for the benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.8(7) the Commission must decide whether the claimant is eligible and whether the benefit is payable, and notify the claimant` IF
    `the Commission has received a claim for the benefit`

§ `Section 153.9 - eligibility`

-- The threshold of (1)(a)(iii) and (1)(c)(iii), and the other figures of this section, are the Act's own.
-- src:2837 | (iii) have insurable earnings of at least $5,000 in 2019 or in the 52 weeks preceding the day on which they make the claim under section 153.8,
-- src:2844 | (iii) have insurable earnings of at least $5,000 in 2019 or within the 52 weeks preceding the day on which they make the claim under section 153.8, and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.9(1)(a)(iii), (c)(iii) (src:2837) (src:2844)
GIVEN `insurable earnings in 2019` IS A NUMBER
      `insurable earnings in the 52 weeks preceding the day on which the claim is made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.9(1)(a)(iii) insurable earnings of at least $5,000` IF
        `insurable earnings in 2019` AT LEAST 5000
     OR `insurable earnings in the 52 weeks preceding the day on which the claim is made` AT LEAST 5000

-- (3): a claimant who leaves their employment voluntarily does not cease working for the purpose of (1).
-- src:2857 | (3) A claimant does not cease working for the purpose of subsection (1) if they leave their employment voluntarily.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.9(3) (src:2857)
GIVEN `ceases working` IS A BOOLEAN
      `leaves their employment voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.9(3) the claimant ceases working for the purpose of subsection (1)` IF
        `ceases working`
    AND NOT (`leaves their employment voluntarily`)

-- (4): income received, from employment or self-employment, of no more than $1,000 in total over four weeks that
-- succeed each other in chronological order but not necessarily consecutively and for which the benefit is paid, is
-- deemed to meet the income requirements. "Receives income" is read as more than nothing (fork F-ei6-4).
-- src:2859 | (4) If a claimant receives income, whether from employment or self-employment, the total of which does not exceed $1,000 over a period of four weeks that succeed each other in chronological order but not necessarily consecutively and in respect of which the employment insurance emergency response benefit is paid, the claimant is deemed to meet the requirements of subparagraphs (1)(a)(iv) and (v), of paragraph (1)(b) or of subparagraph (1)(c)(iv), as the case may be.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.9(4) (src:2859)
GIVEN `the total income from employment and self-employment over the four weeks for which the benefit is paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.9(4) the claimant is deemed to meet the requirements on ceasing work and on income` IF
        `the total income from employment and self-employment over the four weeks for which the benefit is paid` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the total income from employment and self-employment over the four weeks for which the benefit is paid` AT MOST 1000

-- (1)(a): a claimant who resides in Canada, is at least 15, has insurable earnings of at least $5,000, ceases working
-- for at least seven consecutive days within the two-week period and has no income in respect of those days.
-- src:2833 | 153.9 (1) A claimant is eligible for the employment insurance emergency response benefit
-- src:2834 | (a) if they
-- src:2835 | (i) reside in Canada,
-- src:2836 | (ii) are at least 15 years of age,
-- src:2837 | (iii) have insurable earnings of at least $5,000 in 2019 or in the 52 weeks preceding the day on which they make the claim under section 153.8,
-- src:2838 | (iv) whether employed or self-employed, cease working for at least seven consecutive days within the two-week period in respect of which they claimed the benefit, and
-- src:2839 | (v) have no income from employment or self-employment in respect of the consecutive days on which they cease working;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.9(1)(a) (src:2833-2839)
GIVEN `resides in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `age in years` IS A NUMBER
      `has insurable earnings of at least $5,000` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant ceases working for the purpose of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the greatest number of consecutive days within the two-week period for which they cease working` IS A NUMBER
      `income from employment or self-employment in respect of those days` IS A NUMBER
      `deemed to meet the requirements of subparagraphs (a)(iv) and (v) by subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.9(1)(a) eligible as a claimant who ceases working` IF
        `resides in Canada`
    AND `age in years` AT LEAST 15
    AND `has insurable earnings of at least $5,000`
    AND (   (    `the claimant ceases working for the purpose of subsection (1)`
             AND `the greatest number of consecutive days within the two-week period for which they cease working` AT LEAST 7
             AND `income from employment or self-employment in respect of those days` EQUALS 0)
         OR `deemed to meet the requirements of subparagraphs (a)(iv) and (v) by subsection (4)`)

-- (1)(b): a claimant referred to in paragraph 153.5(2)(b) with no income for at least seven consecutive days within
-- the two-week period.
-- src:2840 | (b) if they are a claimant referred to in paragraph 153.5(2)(b) and they have no income from employment or self-employment for at least seven consecutive days within the two-week period in respect of which they claimed the benefit; or
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.9(1)(b) (src:2840)
GIVEN `a claimant referred to in paragraph 153.5(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the greatest number of consecutive days within the two-week period with no income from employment or self-employment` IS A NUMBER
      `deemed to meet the requirements of paragraph (b) by subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.9(1)(b) eligible as a claimant who could have had a benefit period established` IF
        `a claimant referred to in paragraph 153.5(2)(b)`
    AND (   `the greatest number of consecutive days within the two-week period with no income from employment or self-employment` AT LEAST 7
         OR `deemed to meet the requirements of paragraph (b) by subsection (4)`)

-- (1)(c): a claimant referred to in paragraph 153.5(2)(c) or (d) who resides in Canada, is at least 15, has insurable
-- earnings of at least $5,000 and has no income for at least seven consecutive days within the two-week period.
-- src:2841 | (c) if they are a claimant referred to in paragraph 153.5(2)(c) or (d) and they
-- src:2842 | (i) reside in Canada,
-- src:2843 | (ii) are at least 15 years of age,
-- src:2844 | (iii) have insurable earnings of at least $5,000 in 2019 or within the 52 weeks preceding the day on which they make the claim under section 153.8, and
-- src:2845 | (iv) have no income from employment or self-employment for at least seven consecutive days within the two-week period in respect of which they claimed the benefit.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.9(1)(c) (src:2841-2845)
GIVEN `a claimant referred to in paragraph 153.5(2)(c) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `resides in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `age in years` IS A NUMBER
      `has insurable earnings of at least $5,000` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the greatest number of consecutive days within the two-week period with no income from employment or self-employment` IS A NUMBER
      `deemed to meet the requirements of subparagraph (c)(iv) by subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.9(1)(c) eligible as a claimant who is unable to start working` IF
        `a claimant referred to in paragraph 153.5(2)(c) or (d)`
    AND `resides in Canada`
    AND `age in years` AT LEAST 15
    AND `has insurable earnings of at least $5,000`
    AND (   `the greatest number of consecutive days within the two-week period with no income from employment or self-employment` AT LEAST 7
         OR `deemed to meet the requirements of subparagraph (c)(iv) by subsection (4)`)

-- (1): paragraphs (a), (b) and (c) are alternatives (the "or" ends paragraph (b)): fork F-ei6-1.
-- src:2833 | 153.9 (1) A claimant is eligible for the employment insurance emergency response benefit
-- src:2840 | (b) if they are a claimant referred to in paragraph 153.5(2)(b) and they have no income from employment or self-employment for at least seven consecutive days within the two-week period in respect of which they claimed the benefit; or
-- src:2841 | (c) if they are a claimant referred to in paragraph 153.5(2)(c) or (d) and they
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.9(1) (src:2833) (src:2840-2841)
GIVEN `eligible under paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `eligible under paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `eligible under paragraph (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.9(1) the claimant meets the conditions of eligibility` IF
       `eligible under paragraph (a)`
    OR `eligible under paragraph (b)`
    OR `eligible under paragraph (c)`

-- (5) and (6): a claimant who received the benefit for a week for which they were not eligible by reason only of
-- paragraph (2)(c) (or (d)) is deemed to have been eligible, despite that paragraph, unless the Commission has
-- informed the Minister under subsection 15(2) of the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act (or 15.1(2) of the
-- Canada Emergency Student Benefit Act) that subsection 15(1) (or 15.1(1)) should not apply to the claimant.
-- src:2861 | (5) If, for any week, a claimant received an employment insurance emergency response benefit for which they were not eligible by reason only of paragraph (2)(c), the claimant, despite that paragraph, is deemed to have been eligible for the benefit unless the Commission has, under subsection 15(2) of the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act, informed the Minister, as defined in section 2 of that Act, that subsection 15(1) of that Act should not apply in respect of the claimant.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.9(5) (src:2861)
GIVEN `received the benefit for the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not eligible for the week by reason only of paragraph (2)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has informed the Minister under subsection 15(2) of the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act that subsection 15(1) should not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.9(5) the claimant is deemed to have been eligible despite paragraph (2)(c)` IF
        `received the benefit for the week`
    AND `not eligible for the week by reason only of paragraph (2)(c)`
    AND NOT (`the Commission has informed the Minister under subsection 15(2) of the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act that subsection 15(1) should not apply`)

-- src:2863 | (6) If, for any week, a claimant received an employment insurance emergency response benefit for which they were not eligible by reason only of paragraph (2)(d), the claimant, despite that paragraph, is deemed to have been eligible for the benefit unless the Commission has, under subsection 15.1(2) of the Canada Emergency Student Benefit Act, informed the Minister, as defined in section 2 of that Act, that subsection 15.1(1) of that Act should not apply in respect of the claimant.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.9(6) (src:2863)
GIVEN `received the benefit for the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not eligible for the week by reason only of paragraph (2)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has informed the Minister under subsection 15.1(2) of the Canada Emergency Student Benefit Act that subsection 15.1(1) should not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.9(6) the claimant is deemed to have been eligible despite paragraph (2)(d)` IF
        `received the benefit for the week`
    AND `not eligible for the week by reason only of paragraph (2)(d)`
    AND NOT (`the Commission has informed the Minister under subsection 15.1(2) of the Canada Emergency Student Benefit Act that subsection 15.1(1) should not apply`)

-- (2) and (2.1): the grounds on which a claimant is not eligible. A ground (c) or (d) is lifted by (5) or (6).
-- src:2847 | (2) A claimant is not eligible if,
-- src:2848 | (a) they receive, under this Act, a benefit other than the employment insurance emergency response benefit;
-- src:2849 | (b) they receive allowances, money or other benefits paid under a provincial plan
-- src:2850 | (i) because of pregnancy, or
-- src:2851 | (ii) because the claimant is caring for one or more of their new-born children, or one or more children placed with them for the purpose of adoption;
-- src:2852 | (c) they receive an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act; or
-- src:2853 | (d) they receive a Canada emergency student benefit under the Canada Emergency Student Benefit Act.
-- src:2854 | Subsequent ineligibility
-- src:2855 | (2.1) A claimant is not eligible if a benefit period established for the claimant — including a benefit period established in respect of benefits payable under Part VIII — begins after the claimant received an employment insurance emergency response benefit or an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.9(2), (2.1) (src:2847-2855)
GIVEN `receives, under this Act, a benefit other than the emergency response benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `receives allowances, money or other benefits paid under a provincial plan because of pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `receives allowances, money or other benefits paid under a provincial plan because of caring for new-born children or children placed for adoption` IS A BOOLEAN
      `receives an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `deemed eligible despite paragraph (2)(c) by subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `receives a Canada emergency student benefit under the Canada Emergency Student Benefit Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `deemed eligible despite paragraph (2)(d) by subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a benefit period established for the claimant begins after the claimant received the emergency response benefit or an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.9(2) a ground of ineligibility applies to the claimant` IF
       `receives, under this Act, a benefit other than the emergency response benefit`
    OR `receives allowances, money or other benefits paid under a provincial plan because of pregnancy`
    OR `receives allowances, money or other benefits paid under a provincial plan because of caring for new-born children or children placed for adoption`
    OR (`receives an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act` AND NOT (`deemed eligible despite paragraph (2)(c) by subsection (5)`))
    OR (`receives a Canada emergency student benefit under the Canada Emergency Student Benefit Act` AND NOT (`deemed eligible despite paragraph (2)(d) by subsection (6)`))
    OR `a benefit period established for the claimant begins after the claimant received the emergency response benefit or an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act`

-- (1) with (2): a claimant is eligible if they meet the conditions of (1) and no ground of (2) or (2.1) applies.
-- src:2833 | 153.9 (1) A claimant is eligible for the employment insurance emergency response benefit
-- src:2847 | (2) A claimant is not eligible if,
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.9(1), (2) (src:2833) (src:2847)
GIVEN `meets the conditions of eligibility in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a ground of ineligibility applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.9 the claimant is eligible for the emergency response benefit` IF
        `meets the conditions of eligibility in subsection (1)`
    AND NOT (`a ground of ineligibility applies`)

§ `Section 153.10 - the amount of the benefit`

-- src:2865 | 153.10 (1) The amount of the employment insurance emergency response benefit for a week is $500.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.10(1) (src:2865)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 153.10(1) the amount of the emergency response benefit for a week` MEANS 500

-- (2) and (3): provincial assistance does not reduce or eliminate the weekly amount; the family supplement of
-- section 16 and subsections 152.17(1) to (4) applies, with the necessary modifications, to the amount. The increase
-- is decided by those sections (pieces ei1 and ei5), so it is a plain input: the weekly amount is $500 plus it.
-- The provincial receipt is a parameter that is deliberately not read.
-- src:2867 | (2) For greater certainty, if a claimant receives, under a provincial Act or any other provincial mechanism, a sum of money or financial aid of any type and in any form, for reasons related to COVID-19, the weekly amount of the employment insurance emergency response benefit will not be reduced or eliminated.
-- src:2869 | (3) Section 16 and subsections 152.17(1) to (4) apply, with the necessary modifications, to the amount of the employment insurance emergency response benefit.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.10(2), (3) (src:2867) (src:2869)
GIVEN `receives under a provincial Act or other provincial mechanism a sum of money or financial aid for reasons related to COVID-19` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the increase to the rate of weekly benefits under section 16 or subsections 152.17(1) to (4)` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: sections 16 and 152.17 (pieces ei1 and ei5)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 153.10 the amount of the emergency response benefit for a week, with the family supplement` IS
    `s 153.10(1) the amount of the emergency response benefit for a week` PLUS `the increase to the rate of weekly benefits under section 16 or subsections 152.17(1) to (4)`

§ `Section 153.11 - the maximum number of weeks`

-- 28 minus the weeks, if any, for which the claimant receives an income support payment under the Canada Emergency
-- Response Benefit Act or a Canada emergency student benefit. The text has no floor: more than 28 such weeks would
-- give a negative maximum, which the text does not answer, so that case is NOTHING (fork F-ei6-6).
-- src:2871 | 153.11 The maximum number of weeks for which the employment insurance emergency response benefit may be paid to a claimant is 28 minus the number of weeks, if any, for which the claimant receives an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act or a Canada emergency student benefit under the Canada Emergency Student Benefit Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.11 (src:2871)
GIVEN `the number of weeks for which the claimant receives an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act or a Canada emergency student benefit under the Canada Emergency Student Benefit Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 153.11 the maximum number of weeks for which the emergency response benefit may be paid` IS
    IF `the number of weeks for which the claimant receives an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act or a Canada emergency student benefit under the Canada Emergency Student Benefit Act` GREATER THAN 28
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (28 MINUS `the number of weeks for which the claimant receives an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act or a Canada emergency student benefit under the Canada Emergency Student Benefit Act`)

-- src:2871 | 153.11 The maximum number of weeks for which the employment insurance emergency response benefit may be paid to a claimant is 28 minus the number of weeks, if any, for which the claimant receives an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act or a Canada emergency student benefit under the Canada Emergency Student Benefit Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.11 (src:2871)
GIVEN `the number of weeks for which the benefit has already been paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks for which the claimant receives an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act or a Canada emergency student benefit under the Canada Emergency Student Benefit Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.11 the benefit may still be paid for another week` IS
    CONSIDER `s 153.11 the maximum number of weeks for which the emergency response benefit may be paid` `the number of weeks for which the claimant receives an income support payment under the Canada Emergency Response Benefit Act or a Canada emergency student benefit under the Canada Emergency Student Benefit Act`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST maximum THEN JUST (`the number of weeks for which the benefit has already been paid` LESS THAN maximum)

§ `Section 153.111 - the Employment Insurance Operating Account`

-- A duty of the Government's accounts, not of the claimant: no seat question. The amount is the Minister of
-- Finance's, so it is a plain input (out of range: nothing; the amount is not in the text).
-- src:2875 | 153.111 There shall be credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account an amount determined by the Minister of Finance that corresponds to the total cost of the employment insurance emergency response benefit under this Act, including all costs related to the benefit and its administration.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.111 (src:2875)
GIVEN `the amount determined by the Minister of Finance that corresponds to the total cost of the employment insurance emergency response benefit under this Act, including all costs related to the benefit and its administration` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 153.111 the amount to be credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account` IS
    `the amount determined by the Minister of Finance that corresponds to the total cost of the employment insurance emergency response benefit under this Act, including all costs related to the benefit and its administration`
